{
  "title": "Preserve the Prior Code Rendering",
  "story": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "e2a49c5daebfd648",
      "text": "Claude review artefact. Written by a Claude Code review of commit 9b57bd4b of RalfBarkow/hyperdoc on 2026-11-01. It is Claude's criticism: not a result of the Riesbeck/Beane Lisp Critic, not an Evaluation Record and not a passed experiment. Every paragraph on this page was written by that review. A reply belongs on the replying person's own site, linking back here."
    },
    {
      "type": "pagefold",
      "id": "4d3d4cf624c3caa9",
      "text": "question"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ca37e6c456479982",
      "text": "Claude review, answers I1: [[Should the Code Method Preserve the Inspector Rendering?]]"
    },
    {
      "type": "pagefold",
      "id": "d39b76000e3be658",
      "text": "claim"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "9724db375bdfe0ba",
      "text": "Claude review, Position A: Yes. The prior rendering of unmarked Code items, Inspector object reference included, is existing behaviour that an opt-in extension should not change unintentionally."
    },
    {
      "type": "pagefold",
      "id": "094d874d20768040",
      "text": "support"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "e06e9c3459845c18",
      "text": "Claude review, A+1, fact, derived: the else branch of the new method renders only the escaped text, while the fallback method also renders a type label and an Inspector object reference to the item. Compare [https://github.com/RalfBarkow/hyperdoc/blob/9b57bd4bb87d92fbf3061b91a42a6f539e18cdb1/dreyeck/src/verified-example.lisp#L160-L166 verified-example.lisp lines 160-166] with [https://github.com/RalfBarkow/hyperdoc/blob/9b57bd4bb87d92fbf3061b91a42a6f539e18cdb1/hyperbook-fedwiki/story-items.lisp#L109-L115 story-items.lisp lines 109-115]."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "69c869b3667a8d88",
      "text": "Claude review, A+2, fact read as assessment, inferred: the comment says ordinary Code \"remains\" a passive source view [https://github.com/RalfBarkow/hyperdoc/blob/9b57bd4bb87d92fbf3061b91a42a6f539e18cdb1/dreyeck/src/verified-example.lisp#L160-L161 verified-example.lisp lines 160-161], and the report calls the prior state the passive default rendering [https://github.com/RalfBarkow/hyperdoc/blob/9b57bd4bb87d92fbf3061b91a42a6f539e18cdb1/docs/trusted-executable-examples.md?plain=1#L33 trusted-executable-examples.md line 33] and says unmarked Code \"bleibt\" a passive, escaped audit view [https://github.com/RalfBarkow/hyperdoc/blob/9b57bd4bb87d92fbf3061b91a42a6f539e18cdb1/docs/trusted-executable-examples.md?plain=1#L115-L116 trusted-executable-examples.md lines 115-116]. Both state continuity, not change; the prior state had a reference."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "3b5bf77c128423a7",
      "text": "Claude review, A+3, fact, derived: the method dispatches on the item type alone [https://github.com/RalfBarkow/hyperdoc/blob/9b57bd4bb87d92fbf3061b91a42a6f539e18cdb1/dreyeck/src/verified-example.lisp#L160-L166 verified-example.lisp lines 160-166], so in an image that has loaded the slice it applies to every page, foreign pages included."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "4d4c89714f5ae631",
      "text": "Claude review, A+4, normative assumption, inferred from two cases: an opt-in extension leaves the items it does not address unchanged; compare the :after method [https://github.com/RalfBarkow/hyperdoc/blob/9b57bd4bb87d92fbf3061b91a42a6f539e18cdb1/dreyeck/work/how-trails-sources.lisp#L72 how-trails-sources.lisp line 72] and the new item type [https://github.com/RalfBarkow/hyperdoc/blob/9b57bd4bb87d92fbf3061b91a42a6f539e18cdb1/dreyeck/src/dita-story-item.lisp#L229 dita-story-item.lisp line 229]."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "fd5b959bb28637d7",
      "text": "Claude review, A+5, assessment, derived: calling the next method in the else branch would restore the prior rendering and leave the marked path untouched [https://github.com/RalfBarkow/hyperdoc/blob/9b57bd4bb87d92fbf3061b91a42a6f539e18cdb1/dreyeck/src/verified-example.lisp#L160-L166 verified-example.lisp lines 160-166]."
    },
    {
      "type": "pagefold",
      "id": "804e1bf8204c14f9",
      "text": "oppose"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "6fe651e53f897b49",
      "text": "Claude review, A-1, fact, observed: the reach is limited; the slice is opt-in and no other system depends on it [https://github.com/RalfBarkow/hyperdoc/blob/9b57bd4bb87d92fbf3061b91a42a6f539e18cdb1/dreyeck.asd#L467-L480 dreyeck.asd lines 467-480]; the Catalog does not load it [https://github.com/RalfBarkow/hyperdoc/blob/9b57bd4bb87d92fbf3061b91a42a6f539e18cdb1/docs/trusted-executable-examples.md?plain=1#L166 trusted-executable-examples.md line 166]."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "1592415a21c4efeb",
      "text": "Claude review, A-2, normative assumption: a fallback method on T is not obviously a contract; a method specialised for one type may replace it [https://github.com/RalfBarkow/hyperdoc/blob/9b57bd4bb87d92fbf3061b91a42a6f539e18cdb1/hyperbook-fedwiki/story-items.lisp#L109-L115 story-items.lisp lines 109-115]."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "74b3c57b46840a69",
      "text": "Claude review, A-3, assessment, no evidence: whether anyone uses the reference on Code items is unknown."
    },
    {
      "type": "pagefold",
      "id": "11733bf251638c8a",
      "text": "~"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ff238b38beceb726",
      "text": "Claude review, note: each move names its kind (fact, assessment or normative assumption) and the warrant of its content (observed, derived, inferred or hypothesized). That a move supports or opposes the position is Claude's argumentative assignment: interpreted, and checked by nothing."
    }
  ],
